# Case E: College Counseling

## Client
- **Mr. Wolanin**, College Counseling Office, Pomfret School.

## Team
- Developers: James Tian, James Lake, Alex Tong, Erin Park, Claire Desrosiers, Mason Gordon. Club lead: Cayden Auyang. Keep this line and `.github/CODEOWNERS` up to date when the team changes.

## Status
- First meeting with Mr. Wolanin held October 9, 2026. Building a first demo.

## The problem
- Before writing each student's recommendation letter, a counselor gathers the student's teacher comments and questionnaire answers by hand into one Google Doc.

## Decisions (do not reopen)
- The counselor writes every letter. The tool only gathers and organizes. Never write or draft letter text: no AI-written letters.
- Adaptive questions come later, only after the counselors approve.

## First deliverable: student profile builder demo
- In: two Google Sheets of made-up data (questionnaire answers; teacher comments with student, course, teacher, term).
- Out: one profile Doc per student, with answers by section, comments grouped by course and term, and an empty "My notes" section the tool never touches.
- Runs from a "Build profiles" menu in Apps Script. A second run updates each Doc without duplicating anything.

## Stack
- Google Apps Script in a Google Sheet, for this deliverable.

## Guidance
- Student data in a college counseling context is sensitive (grades, essays, recommendations). Never commit real student data, exports, or documents to this repo; use made-up sample data and say so in the README.
- Never commit Sheet or Doc IDs or web app links. Add a `.env.example` the moment any credential or ID is needed.
